PYTHON DOCKER FILE AND NODEJS DOCKER FILE IS MOSTLY SIMILAR.

FROM node
WORKDIR /myapp
COPY package*.json ./
RUN npm install
COPY . .
EXPOSE 3000       //GIVE THE PORT BASED ON OUR APPLICATION WHAT YOUR MENTONED
CMD ["npm","src/server.js"] (here give the path where the source code. Here the js file in src that's why I gave src/server.js. EXAMPLE IF YOU HAVE THE JS FILE IN ROOR DIRCTORY THEN FIVE ONLY SERVER.JS OR INDEX.JS BASED ON YOUR FILE NAME)


NOW BUILD THE IMAGE AND CREATE THE CONTAINER TO ACCES THE APPLICATION

BUILD IMAGE: dokcer build -t nodejs-image:v1 .
CREATE CONTAINER: docker run -itd --name nodejs-cont -p 1133:3000 nodejs-image:v1

